Flow Traders::gh_flowtraders_8173418.description:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Are you ready for two days on a real trading floor?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Join the Flow Quant Trading Days at our Amsterdam office on 7 &amp;amp; 8 December 2026 - a hands-on quant trading academy for a select group of 15 students. Find out whether trading is for you with an exciting look inside our Trading floor, and the chance to receive a full-time job offer as a Graduate Trader.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Over two days you&#39;ll price, arbitrage and hedge in live simulations, make markets under real time pressure, and go head-to-head with our traders in games built to test your instinct. You will have the opportunity to show your curiosity while shadowing the trading desks, watching news as it hits the market.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What&#39;s in it for you?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An insight into trading at Flow Traders;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Introductory classes on traditional finance, Crypto and ETFs;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on simulations where you can show your competitive spirit;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Desk shadowing in small groups;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Games night to demonstrate your trading intuition - where you’ll go head-to-head with our traders;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Our in-house facilities: gym with personal trainers, bar, barista, arcade room, and a lounge with daily catered lunches from our chef;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dinner in Amsterdam and farewell drinks in the Flow Bar with the trading team;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;And of course, the chance to receive a full-time job offer as a Graduate Trader.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Do you have what it takes?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Are you graduating in 2026 or 2027 from a BSc/MSc STEM degree in the Netherlands, with a demonstrable interest in trading on your CV? Do you code - Python or otherwise - and enjoy reasoning with probabilities and brainteasers? Can you spot an opportunity, and are you assertive enough to seize it? We&#39;re looking for competitive, curious and entrepreneurial students.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The application procedure &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We invite you to apply through our website by submitting your resume as well as a persuasive cover letter. The application deadline will be &lt;strong&gt;November 13&lt;sup&gt;th&lt;/sup&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Flow Traders does not accept unsolicited resumes from any professional staffing or search firms. All resumes, and any other information identifying potential candidates, submitted to any employee at Flow Traders via-email, the Internet or directly without a valid and signed search agreement will be deemed free to contact by Flow Traders without any restrictions and no placement fee of any kind will be paid in the event the candidate is hired by Flow Traders.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

Old Mission Capital::gh_oldmissioncapita.description:
&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Old Mission is a global proprietary trading firm that leverages state-of-the-art technology and research to identify and execute profitable trading strategies across multiple asset classes around the world. Our offices in Chicago, New York, and London are all composed of naturally-curious individuals who thrive in a team environment and constantly strive for improvement.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About The Position&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Old Mission Capital, a quantitative proprietary trading firm, is currently recruiting a Junior Quantitative Trader (Asian Market hours) to join our Chicago office. Our traders work in teams to seek out and profitably trade mispriced securities. The junior trader needs to be driven and have a passion for understanding how things work. The job responsibilities will include disciplined decision making, risk management, derivative pricing, and researching new opportunities for profitable businesses.&amp;nbsp;Passion for trading is critical! Besides meeting the qualifications the most successful candidates will have a strong desire to understand how things work. You should have a deep interest in the financial markets and want to join a collaborative team. We value each other’s ideas and have the mindset to continuously improve and build towards the future.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor systems and manage all trading activity between Sunday – Thursday from 4:00 pm – 3:00 am CST.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee and manage the trade execution and risk of complex trading portfolios across the firm.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement trading strategies that leverage technology to efficiently execute trades at minimum transactional costs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research potential trading opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A degree in a quantitative field such as computer science, engineering, or one of the hard sciences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with at least one of the following languages: Python, C++, JAVA, VBA, R, Matlab or Ruby&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of relevant trading experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced with automated trading systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven trustworthiness and performance under the highest ethical standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to solve problems in a high-pressure environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Superior written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must be self-motivated, dependable, responsible and results driven.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain integrity at all times.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A desire to work Asian market hours. Work hours will include US holidays if the international markets are open.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong work ethic and ability to adapt quickly in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits and Perks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully paid Medical, Dental, Vision, Disability, and Life Insurance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully stocked kitchen; free breakfast and lunch every day on-site&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tuition Reimbursement Program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;401(k) with employer match&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Paid Vacation, Sick, and Parental leaves&lt;/li&gt;
