&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Summary:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a Senior Platform Engineer to help build, operate, and improve the software delivery and developer infrastructure platforms used by engineering teams working on large-scale C++ and Python applications. This role combines platform engineering, CI/CD, build systems, infrastructure automation, observability, artifact management, and developer productivity. The ideal candidate has strong systems engineering fundamentals and practical experience supporting complex engineering workflows in a production-critical environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Designing, building, and enhancing tools that support developer productivity, systems infrastructure, and DevOps practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with the global Platform, Developer Infrastructure, and Release Engineering team to align regional solutions with global standards while representing local engineering, operational, and business priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain and improve build and release infrastructure for large-scale C++ and Python applications, including build tooling, dependency management, CI/CD integration, artifact workflows, and developer self-service capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with software engineers, infrastructure engineers, quants, traders, and SRE teams to design, build, and operate reliable software delivery platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, develop, and operate scalable CI/CD pipelines for build, test, artifact promotion, deployment, and release workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain infrastructure automation and configuration management solutions for platform, CI/CD, artifact, and developer infrastructure services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop internal developer tooling and self-service platform capabilities that reduce operational toil and improve developer productivity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use containerization and orchestration technologies to support reproducible builds, reliable CI/CD execution, and consistent deployment workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve observability for build, CI/CD, release, and platform services through centralized logging, metrics, tracing, dashboards, and alerting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot and optimize build, CI/CD, artifact, and developer infrastructure systems with a focus on performance, reliability, scalability, and security.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement software supply chain security practices, including artifact provenance, dependency management, vulnerability scanning, secret management, and CI/CD security controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in incident response, root cause analysis, and continuous improvement for platform-owned build, release, CI/CD, and developer infrastructure services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and recommend improvements to build, release, CI/CD, developer infrastructure, observability, and software delivery platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or a related discipline, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of hands-on engineering experience building, operating, or improving software delivery, platform, infrastructure, CI/CD, DevOps, SRE, or developer productivity systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Linux systems knowledge and troubleshooting skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of software build systems, especially for large C++ codebases; experience with CMake, Ninja, Bazel, Buck2, or similar tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Python packaging, dependency management, and environment management tools such as pip, conda, uv, pixi, or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building and operating CI/CD platforms, including pipeline design, build/test automation, artifact promotion, secrets handling, and failure diagnosis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with artifact repositories, binary/package distribution, and artifact lifecycle management using tools such as Artifactory, Nexus, Harbor, or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with infrastructure automation and configuration management tools such as Terraform, Ansible, or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with containerization technologies such as Docker or Podman; familiarity with orchestration platforms such as Kubernetes, Nomad, ECS, or similar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with cloud, hybrid, or on-premises infrastructure environments; AWS, GCP, Azure, or private infrastructure experience preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Python and shell scripting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Git and collaborative development workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of networking fundamentals, including DNS, load balancing, TLS, HTTP, routing, and service discovery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical understanding of distributed systems reliability concepts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience gathering developer feedback and translating recurring pain points into self-service tooling, automation, documentation, or platform improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with the ability to work in a fast-paced, globally distributed engineering environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and collaboration skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Experience with:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshooting C++ build, linkage, dependency, ABI, compiler, linker, and toolchain issues in large codebases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Modernizing legacy build systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improving build reproducibility, reducing build times, or introducing remote caching / remote execution.&lt;/li&gt;
