Cubist Systematic Strategies::gh_point72.description:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Career with Point72&#39;s Steven &amp;amp; Alexandra Cohen Foundation/Office of Inclusion and Community Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Steven &amp;amp; Alexandra Cohen Foundation is a nonprofit organization committed to inspiring philanthropy and community service, leading by example to show the world what giving can do. Working closely with the Foundation, the Office of Inclusion &amp;amp; Community is the engine that drives the philanthropic culture and strong sense of community among the employees of Point72, a global asset management company.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create high-quality, on-brand digital collateral for social media, web, and external communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Shape visual narratives for reports and presentations, translating data and philanthropic impact into polished layouts, graphics, and design systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain Foundation and Community websites through content edits, page creation, and visual updates using the Amazin’ Mets Foundation’s content management system.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support communications plans and programs that advance the Amazin’ Mets Foundation’s mission and the philanthropic vision of its leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organize communications materials, including press releases, media advisories, annual reports, and coverage summaries that reinforce the Foundation’s story.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage mailing lists, distribution, and engagement tracking for internal and external communications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build content calendars for social and digital channels, coordinating creation, and delivery across the year.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze campaign performance and quarterly reporting, identifying insights that improve audience engagement and strengthen future storytelling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply artificial intelligence and automation tools to streamline monitoring, reporting, and data tracking while reducing manual processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with internal and external creators, including designers, video editors, Mets photographers, and production teams, to deliver compelling content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What&#39;s required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of digital communications experience, including social media and visual content creation for digital platforms and print materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong portfolio demonstrating visual storytelling, digital design, and brand-aligned creative work across channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with Adobe Creative Cloud, Canva, Microsoft Office, and digital communications platforms including Mailchimp, Hootsuite, and Classy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong digital copywriting, written and verbal communication, and editorial judgment to identify high-quality content opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience shooting and editing video and photos.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent organization and project management skills, with the ability to meet deadlines and manage multiple priorities in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound judgment, discretion, and attention to detail when handling sensitive information and fast-moving situations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work flexible hours, including nights, weekends, and holidays, with some local and non-local travel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitment to the highest ethical standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We take care of our people&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We invest in our people, their careers, their health, and their well-being. When you work here, we provide:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully-paid health care benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous parental and family leave policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Volunteer opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support for employee-led affinity groups representing women, people of color and the LGBT+ community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental and physical wellness programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tuition assistance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A 401(k) savings program with an employer match and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Point72&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Point72 is a leading global alternative investment firm led by Steven A. Cohen. Building on more than 30 years of investing experience, Point72 seeks to deliver superior returns for its investors through fundamental and systematic investing strategies across asset classes and geographies. We aim to attract and retain the industry&#39;s brightest talent by cultivating an investor-led culture and committing to our people&#39;s long-term growth. For more information, visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://point72.com/&quot;&gt;https://point72.com/&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The annual base salary range for this role is $90,000-$100,000 (USD) , which does not include discretionary bonus compensation or our comprehensive benefits package. Actual compensation offered to the successful candidate may vary from posted hiring range based upon geographic location, work experience, education, and/or skill level, among other things.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Career with Point72’s Investment Professional Engagement Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Investment Professional Engagement (IPE) team is dedicated to helping our investment professionals build durable careers and become better investors. Working in close partnership with teams across the Fundamental Equities business, IPE builds capabilities at the intersection of talent cultivation and technology by creating and delivering content and training, driving adoption of the firm&#39;s tools, and supporting the long-term career progression of our investment talent.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with coaches and other subject matter experts across Fundamental Equities management to turn their ideas, frameworks, and methods into clear, practical content for investment professionals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create stock case studies based on realistic long/short investment setups, distilling complex situations into rigorous, teachable materials without losing the nuance that makes them useful&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and maintain a library of investment frameworks, research guides, templates, checklists, worked examples, and other resources that reflect how fundamental research is done at the desk&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keep materials current as markets, companies, research approaches, and analyst workflows evolve, while maintaining consistent standards for quality and usability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with technology and AI teams to translate approved tools into practical research applications and coaching content that can make workflows more effective&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Compliance on the appropriate use of live tickers, third-party data, proprietary information, and AI tools in created materials&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support content roadmaps for various teams by identifying gaps, anticipating new needs, and helping prioritize and deliver the materials that will have the greatest impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build strong relationships across investment, coaching, technology, and Fundamental Equities management teams to align perspectives and drive projects forward&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What’s required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience as a fundamental long/short equities analyst at a hedge fund&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong command of fundamental investment research, including variant perception, earnings and valuation analysis, catalysts, risk-reward assessment, and thesis monitoring&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to identify materials and tools for investment professionals that are credible, relevant, and useful at the desk&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working understanding of AI tools, including large language models, agentic workflows, and document-retrieval systems, and how they support the fundamental research process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to translate complex investment concepts into clear, accessible language and turn direction into plans that build alignment across stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven success managing multiple assignments, prioritizing effectively, and consistently producing high-quality work in a demanding, fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Discretion and sound judgement when working with proprietary or sensitive information&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitment to the highest ethical standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We take care of our people&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We invest in our people, their careers, their health, and their well-being. When you work here, we provide:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully-paid health care benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous parental and family leave policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Volunteer opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support for employee-led affinity groups representing women, people of color and the LGBT+ community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental and physical wellness programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tuition assistance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A 401(k) savings program with an employer match and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Point72&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Point72 is a leading global alternative investment firm led by Steven A. Cohen. Building on more than 30 years of investing experience, Point72 seeks to deliver superior returns for its investors through fundamental and systematic investing strategies across asset classes and geographies. We aim to attract and retain the industry’s brightest talent by cultivating an investor-led culture and committing to our people’s long-term growth. For more information, visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://point72.com/&quot;&gt;https://point72.com/&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The annual base salary range for this role is $175,000-$225,000 (USD) , which does not include discretionary bonus compensation or our comprehensive benefits package. Actual compensation offered to the successful candidate may vary from posted hiring range based upon geographic location, work experience, education, and/or skill level, among other things.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Career with Point72&#39;s Technology Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As Point72 reimagines the future of investing, our Technology team is constantly evolving our firm’s IT infrastructure and engineering capabilities, positioning us at the forefront of a rapidly evolving technology landscape. We’re a team of experts who experiment and work to discover new ways to harness open-source solutions, modern cloud architectures, and sophisticated Artificial Intelligence (AI) solutions, while embracing enterprise agile methodologies. Our commitment to building and innovating in the AI space provides the framework intended to drive smarter decision making and enhance how we build and operate our platforms and applications.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a member of Point72’s Technology team, we encourage and support your professional development from day one—helping you advance your technical skills, contribute innovative ideas, and satisfy your own intellectual curiosity—all while delivering real business impact for our multi-billion-dollar global business.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT YOU&#39;LL DO&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement high-performance infrastructure to support large-scale generative AI and machine learning workloads, enabling faster model iteration and real business impact&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and operate distributed systems for model training, hyperparameter tuning, inference, and data preprocessing pipelines to deliver reliable end-to-end machine learning (ML) workflows&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with ML researchers and engineers to produce models, optimizing compute utilization, training throughput, and inference latency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and automate deployment, orchestration, and CI/CD pipelines for models and data workflows using container orchestration and infrastructure-as-code (IaC)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement observability, monitoring, and cost-management strategies for GPU and accelerator compute environments to maintain predictable performance and spend&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate, integrate, and benchmark emerging hardware and software technologies across cloud and on-prem environments to improve scalability and throughput&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive security, compliance, and operational runbooks for GenAI infrastructure including access controls, secrets management, and incident response procedures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot, profile, and optimize performance across GPU and CPU compute stacks to remove bottlenecks and increase reliability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document architecture, operational practices, and mentor engineers to expand team capability and accelerate adoption of production-ready GenAI infrastructure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WHAT&#39;S REQUIRED&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s or master&#39;s degree in computer science, electrical engineering, or a related technical field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–7 years of experience building and maintaining scalable compute or machine learning infrastructure systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of distributed systems, container orchestration (Kubernetes), and public cloud platforms such as AWS, Google Cloud Platform, or Azure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience with machine learning operations and infrastructure tools such as MLflow, Ray, Airflow, Kubeflow, and Terraform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of reinforcement learning concepts and their infrastructure implications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in Python and systems-level programming in one or more languages such as Go, C++, or Rust&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong debugging, performance profiling, and optimization skills across GPU and CPU compute stacks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience implementing monitoring, observability, and cost-optimization for GPU/accelerator-based compute environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent collaboration and communication skills with a systems-thinking mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitment to the highest ethical standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;WE TAKE CARE OF OUR PEOPLE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We invest in our people, their careers, their health, and their well-being. When you work here, we provide:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fully-paid health care benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous parental and family leave policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Volunteer opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support for employee-led affinity groups representing women, people of color and the LGBT+ community&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mental and physical wellness programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tuition assistance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A 401(k) savings program with an employer match and more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT POINT72&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Point72 is a leading global alternative investment firm led by Steven A. Cohen. Building on more than 30 years of investing experience, Point72 seeks to deliver superior returns for its investors through fundamental and systematic investing strategies across asset classes and geographies. We aim to attract and retain the industry&#39;s brightest talent by cultivating an investor-led culture and committing to our people&#39;s long-term growth. For more information, visit https://point72.com/.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The annual base salary range for this role is $180,000-$300,000 (USD) , which does not include discretionary bonus compensation or our comprehensive benefits package. Actual compensation offered to the successful candidate may vary from posted hiring range based upon geographic location, work experience, education, and/or skill level, among other things.&lt;/p&gt;
