Point72::point72_8811167002.description:
&lt;h1&gt;A Career with Investment Services at Point72&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Investment Services colleagues are subject-matter experts who excel in their fields, comprise more than half our firm, and are critical to our success. As strategic partners, they support our investment professionals across areas including strategy, operations, finance, technology, compliance, tax, HR and legal. Everyone on every team has the opportunity to make an impact on our business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;About the Investment Services Internship&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are interested in pursuing a career in the corporate functions of a leading global alternative investment firm, this 10-week summer internship will provide you with valuable, hands-on experience at a complex global firm. You will gain exposure to the fast-paced, competitive hedge fund industry alongside senior professionals dedicated to your success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to the learning and development you&#39;ll receive in your day-to-day role with your team, as part of our summer internship program you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work alongside your fellow interns and be mentored by experienced professionals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meet your peers through designated intern programming, volunteer opportunities, and social events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attend sessions with senior leaders discussing their expertise and career paths&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have hands-on access to best-in-class tools and resources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gain exposure to groups and functions with unique responsibilities and perspectives on our industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop your technical, writing, and presentation skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;When you apply to our internship program, you will be considered for a variety of teams based on your interests and experience and our business needs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;What&#39;s Required&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently pursuing a bachelor&#39;s degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in the asset management industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple tasks and deadlines in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical, writing, verbal communication, and technical skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to work cooperatively with all levels of the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate professionalism and integrity in all interactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitment to the highest ethical standards&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Team Overviews&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Corporate Communications team manages the global reputation of Point72 and all related entities. The team is responsible for all aspects of corporate communications, including media relations, external and internal communications, digital content and distribution, and brand management. This team works closely with Point72 senior management, functional leaders, and all departments firmwide.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Compliance department is an industry-leading team of compliance professionals who support global investment and trading activities by establishing and enforcing the firm&#39;s compliance policies, providing real-time advice, and conducting pre- and post-trade surveillance.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Facilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;MuiPaper-root MuiPaper-elevation MuiPaper-rounded MuiPaper-elevation0 MuiAccordion-root MuiAccordion-rounded Mui-expanded MuiAccordion-gutters css-ydipq2&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;MuiCollapse-root MuiCollapse-vertical MuiCollapse-entered css-1cbf1l2&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;MuiCollapse-wrapper MuiCollapse-vertical css-15830to&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;MuiCollapse-wrapperInner MuiCollapse-vertical css-9vd5ud&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;MuiAccordion-region css-1xdhyk6&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;MuiAccordionDetails-root css-l9xe8y&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body2 css-yhcg9n&quot;&gt;The Facilities team delivers a high level of corporate services to our offices around the globe, including real estate, property management, construction project management, day-to-day operations, maintenance, and security.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;MuiFormControl-root MuiFormControl-fullWidth css-17qa0m8&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Finance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Finance team provides a broad range of timely, accurate, relevant, and objective financial information, advice, and services to its business partners across Corporate Accounting, Global Payments, Procurement, FP&amp;amp;A, and Financial Reporting, with commitment to the highest professional and ethical standards.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Human Capital&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an HR Team, our mission is to be trusted business partners and advisors within the Point72 community, committed to driving a distinctive culture that values collaboration, innovation, and adaptive performance. We are a group of professionals who prioritize business context while listening to all sides, across teams and levels, with empathy. We strive to be commercial and innovative, focused on deeply understand the nuances of global and business unit dynamics and seeking unconventional ways of approaching our relationships with our people.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Legal&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Legal team&#39;s mission is to deliver exceptional legal services in a manner that promotes the firm&#39;s performance with the utmost integrity. Our Legal department supports all Point72 groups globally with practical advice on a variety of complex legal and regulatory matters in an ever-changing, dynamic environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Risk&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Operational Risk group is responsible for identification, monitoring, and reporting of operational risk across the firm. We also manage business continuity, third-party risks, and commercial lines of insurance (excluding employee benefits).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Operations team supports all operational aspects of trade processing, reconciliation, financing, and reporting firmwide for all products, including equities, derivatives, bonds, foreign exchange and futures, and digital assets across global markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regulatory Reporting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Regulatory Reporting team provides governance across all regulatory filings and related obligations globally. The team is responsible for report preparation, generating and coordinating responses for large cross-departmental filings, oversight of technology supporting regulatory filings, identification and implementation automation opportunities, and administering data standards. Regulators include but are not limited to the Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC), Commodity Futures Trading Commission (CFTC), National Futures Association (NFA), Monetary Authority of Singapore (MAS), Financial Conduct Authority (FCA), Securities and Futures Commission (SFC), and Kanto Finance Bureau (KFB).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Implementation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Strategic Implementation team drives the end-to-end delivery of large-scale, cross-functional initiatives that enable business growth and effective change management in alignment with the firm&#39;s long-term vision. Partnering with leaders across the firm, the team ensures alignment, operational readiness, and thoughtful risk management for new business activities and enterprise programs at every stage. The team plays a critical role in delivering the programs that fuel growth, innovation, and operational excellence firmwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Strategy team is a multidisciplinary group that partners directly with the firm&#39;s businesses to identify, design, and lead value-creating strategic business initiatives. We enable the development of new businesses, engage in special projects, and support the firm&#39;s strategic planning process. We also source, negotiate, and manage the firm&#39;s data assets, building a unified foundation that supports our investment professionals and the firm&#39;s growing data and AI ambitions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Treasury&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Treasury team supports the firm&#39;s credit and treasury functions across Central Funding, Securities Lending, and Broker Relations—verifying and disputing margin calls, reporting on counterparty exposure, investing excess cash, and negotiating margin terms with prime brokers and derivative counterparts. This work spans a range of asset classes, including equities, derivatives, bonds, foreign exchange, and futures, across global markets.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;About Point72&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Point72 is a leading global alternative investment firm led by Steven A. Cohen. Building on more than 30 years of investing experience, Point72 seeks to deliver superior returns for its investors through fundamental and systematic investing strategies across asset classes and geographies. We aim to attract and retain the industry&#39;s brightest talent by cultivating an investor-led culture and committing to our people&#39;s long-term growth. For more information, visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://point72.com/&quot;&gt;https://point72.com/&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The annual base salary is $75,000 (USD) which will be prorated based on internship start and end date. Actual compensation offered to the successful candidate may vary from posted hiring based upon geographic location, work experience, education, and/or skill level, among other things.&lt;/p&gt;

Point72::point72_8375256002.description:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Payroll Specialist, United States Payroll&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Career with Point72’s Finance Team &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Finance team provides a broad range of timely, accurate, relevant, and objective financial information, advice, and services to its business partners, with commitment to the highest professional and ethical standards. Our team offers a dynamic and collaborative environment where our colleagues can learn at a fast pace and are rewarded with advanced opportunities both within Finance and across the firm.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Payroll Specialist for the U.S. Payroll who will have direct ownership of hands-on payroll processing in addition to providing subject matter expertise and oversight. Specifically, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end U.S. payroll processing with minimal supervision, including data gathering, validation, review, and final sign-off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead complex payroll activities such as multi-state tax calculations, W-2 testing and reconciliation, 401(k) processing, salary variance analysis, and retroactive adjustments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the U.S. payroll subject matter expert, providing guidance on federal, state, and local tax matters and ensuring compliance and accuracy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently prepare, review, and post payroll journal entries, including accruals, reversals, and adjustments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the primary point of contact for payroll escalations, employee inquiries, client questions, and external vendor coordination&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Human Resources (HR), Finance, Tax, and Benefits teams to resolve payroll issues, support audits, and manage cross-functional dependencies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review payroll outputs for quality and compliance, proactively identifying, investigating, and remediating discrepancies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive payroll process improvements, automation, system enhancements, and transitions using tools such as Excel, Workday, and other reporting/automation solutions, while mentoring junior team members as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What’s required? &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree or equivalent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of finance, accounting, and/or U.S. payroll experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong hands-on expertise in state and local tax calculations and compliance, W-2 testing, year-end reconciliation, and corrections, 401(k) and benefits-related payroll processing, and salary variance analysis, reconciliations, and exception handling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced MS Excel proficiency, including VLOOKUP and XLOOKUP, COUNTIFS and SUMIFS, and nested IFs and complex reconciliation logic&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of US federal, state, and other jurisdictional payroll taxes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced experience with payroll-related journal entries, accruals, and financial reconciliations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to independently collect, validate, and review payroll data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing payroll for foreign or global clients or working within a global service delivery model&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent attention to detail with a process-oriented approach to payroll compensation for some of the top leading professionals in the industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to efficiently analyze sizeable amounts of data and work with the Technology team to identify opportunities where improvement is essential&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to excel in a dynamic, fast paced environment and work effectively under pressure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A willingness to manage change and build working relationships with our clients within Finance and throughout the firm&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong verbal and written communication skills (English language verbal and writing skills)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent organizational skills to meet deadlines and manage multiple priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitment to the highest ethical standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT POINT72 &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Point72 is a leading global alternative investment firm led by Steven A. Cohen. Building on more than 30 years of investing experience, Point72 seeks to deliver superior returns for its investors through fundamental and systematic investing strategies across asset classes and geographies. We aim to attract and retain the industry’s brightest talent by cultivating an investor-led culture and committing to our people’s long-term growth. For more information, visit https://point72.com/&lt;/p&gt;

Tower Research Capital::gh_towerresearch.description:
&lt;p&gt;Tower Research Capital is a leading quantitative trading firm founded in 1998. Tower has built its business on a high-performance platform and independent trading teams. We have a 25+ year track record of innovation and a reputation&amp;nbsp; for discovering unique market opportunities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tower is home to some of the world’s best systematic trading and engineering talent. We empower portfolio managers to build their teams and strategies independently while providing the economies of scale that come from a large, global organization.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Engineers thrive at Tower while developing electronic trading infrastructure at a world class level. Our engineers solve challenging problems in the realms of low-latency programming, FPGA technology, hardware acceleration and machine learning. Our ongoing investment in top engineering talent and technology ensures our platform remains unmatched in terms of functionality, scalability and performance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tower, every employee plays a role in our success. Our Business Support teams are essential to building and maintaining the platform that powers everything we do — combining market access, data, compute, and research infrastructure with risk management, compliance, and a full suite of business services. Our Business Support teams enable our trading and engineering teams to perform at their best.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tower, employees will find a stimulating, results-oriented environment where highly intelligent and motivated colleagues inspire each other to reach their greatest potential.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Performing end-to-end processing of monthly multi-country payrolls in India and APAC (Singapore, China, Hong Kong, Australia and Japan) including scheduling and timelines, collection of information, analysis, input, reconciliation, funding, reporting and follow-up&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Keeping the regional and global team abreast of changing payroll and benefits laws in country&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Completing and auditing tax filings as required by government&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Producing payroll and compensation reports as scheduled for various departments and assisting with participation in special surveys&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;General ledger reporting process including preparing, auditing, and delivering files to Accounting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinating with HR for onboarding, offboarding, and maintaining the relevant systems for electronic personnel and compensation data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collecting and processing new hire documentation and maintaining employee files to ensure compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensuring labor law compliances are adhered to in the region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Helping strategize on payroll best practice, and implementing policy/procedures that ensure ongoing risk controls&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owning the Payroll and Benefits email inbox, and being the first point of contact to assist employees with daily questions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assisting with the annual benefits renewal and enrollment process, and liaising with vendors to resolve employee benefit matters and maintain data integrity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Preparing monthly benefits reports for 3rd party insurers, and auditing/processing monthly invoices (GTL, GPA, Health Insurance etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reviewing benefits carrier connection uploads and investigating any errors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working with the global team and consultants to find valuable benefit plans for the Tower companies in the APAC and India region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Supporting our global benefits initiative by competitive marketing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Providing demographic information, and analytics to that will be used to manage the global benefits platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinating and delivering benefits information sessions and workshops for new hires, annual enrollment and ongoing benefits acclimation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Producing and auditing benefits billing reconciliations and assist with participation in special surveys&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensuring benefits compliance according to country laws&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Managing the data integrity of 3rd party vendor data (i.e., health census data, enrollments, salaries for life assurance coverage)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serving as a liaison with benefits providers to help resolve employee claims&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of HR experience in Payroll and Benefits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Specific knowledge of APAC/India payroll is a must&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of Workday is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Payroll and/or benefits implementation experience a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to execute processes and tasks with little supervision&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to maintain confidentiality and respond effectively to such situations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills and ability to simplify complex payroll and benefits material&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong Excel skills and knowledge of any well-known payroll and benefits systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Aptitude to learn and understand new software and applications quickly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tower’s headquarters are in the historic Equitable Building, right in the heart of NYC’s Financial District and our impact is global, with over a dozen offices around the world.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tower, we believe work should be both challenging and enjoyable. That is why we foster a culture where smart, driven people thrive – without the egos. Our open concept workplace, casual dress code, and well-stocked kitchens reflect the value we place on a friendly, collaborative environment where everyone is respected, and great ideas win.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our benefits include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous paid time off policies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Savings plans and other financial wellness tools available in each region&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hybrid working opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free breakfast, lunch, and snacks daily&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;In-office wellness experiences and reimbursement for select wellness expenses (e.g., gym, personal training and more)&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Company-sponsored sports teams and fitness events (JPM Corporate Challenge, Cycle for Survival, Wall Street Rides FAR and more)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Volunteer opportunities and charitable giving&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Social events, happy hours, treats, and celebrations throughout the year&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Workshops and continuous learning opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Tower, you’ll find a collaborative and welcoming culture, a diverse team and a workplace that values both performance and enjoyment. No unnecessary hierarchy. No ego. Just great people doing great work – together.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Tower Research Capital is an equal opportunity employer.&lt;/p&gt;

Schonfeld Strategic Advisors::gh_schonfe.description:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;The Role&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking to hire a Junior Compliance Associate to join our London office. This role will report into the Global Head of Core Compliance and hold primary responsibility for the day-to-day execution, maintenance, and continuous improvement of the Firm&#39;s policies and procedures framework.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This position requires a focus on high levels of accuracy, consistency, and organizational discipline. It requires a blend of strong writing ability, governance knowledge, and a proactive approach to document management and process improvement. In addition to the primary policies and procedures remit, this role will contribute to core compliance activities as part of a broader global compliance team and necessitates flexibility to support the wider compliance department with activities outside of the listed responsibilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the end-to-end policy lifecycle – identifying gaps, drafting and editing documents in collaboration with policy owners, and maintaining a comprehensive, version-controlled policy library.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Standardize language, structure, and formatting across the policy suite, ensuring consistent cross-document references and hyperlinks throughout the framework.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track document updates, manage review schedules, and ensure all changes are appropriately authorized, providing regular progress updates to management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maximize the use of automation and AI to improve the efficiency and scalability of the policy management function.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to core compliance activities as part of the global compliance team, including Code of Ethics monitoring, review and assessments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be an integral and collaborative member of the London compliance team and broader global Compliance department.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;What you&#39;ll bring&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;What you need:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree or equivalent.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional written English with the ability to produce clear, concise, and well-structured documents; strong editorial and proofreading skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly self-motivated, organized, and attentive to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structured, methodical, and consistent in execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Calm and concise communicator, collaborative and able to engage well with staff of varying roles and seniority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable with technology, systems, and process-oriented ways of working.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;d love if you had:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AI-powered writing tools, content management systems, or workflow automation platforms (e.g. Microsoft Copilot, Power Automate, or similar).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience of adopting workflow management toolkits and new technologies to drive efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Project management skills and experience working with document management platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Who We Are&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Schonfeld is a global multi-manager hedge fund that strives to deliver industry-leading risk-adjusted returns for our investors. We leverage both internal and external portfolio manager teams around the world, seeking to capitalize on inefficiencies and opportunities within the markets. We draw from decades of experience and a significant investment in proprietary technology, infrastructure and risk analytics to invest across four main strategies: Quant, Tactical, Fundamental Equity and Discretionary Macro &amp;amp; Fixed Income.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Our Culture&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Schonfeld, we’ll invest in you. Attracting and retaining top talent is at the heart of what we do, because we believe that exceptional outcomes begin with exceptional people. We foster a culture where talent is empowered to continually learn, innovate and pursue ambitious goals. We are teamwork-oriented, collaborative and encourage ideas—at all levels—to be shared. As an organization committed to investing in our people, we provide learning and educational offerings and opportunities to make an impact. We encourage community through internal networks, external partnerships and service initiatives that promote inclusion and purpose beyond the firm’s walls.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

Cubist Systematic Strategies::gh_point72.description:
&lt;h1&gt;A Career with Investment Services at Point72&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Investment Services colleagues are subject-matter experts who excel in their fields, comprise more than half our firm, and are critical to our success. As strategic partners, they support our investment professionals across areas including strategy, operations, finance, technology, compliance, tax, HR and legal. Everyone on every team has the opportunity to make an impact on our business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;About the Investment Services Internship&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you are interested in pursuing a career in the corporate functions of a leading global alternative investment firm, this 10-week summer internship will provide you with valuable, hands-on experience at a complex global firm. You will gain exposure to the fast-paced, competitive hedge fund industry alongside senior professionals dedicated to your success.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to the learning and development you&#39;ll receive in your day-to-day role with your team, as part of our summer internship program you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work alongside your fellow interns and be mentored by experienced professionals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Meet your peers through designated intern programming, volunteer opportunities, and social events&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attend sessions with senior leaders discussing their expertise and career paths&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have hands-on access to best-in-class tools and resources&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gain exposure to groups and functions with unique responsibilities and perspectives on our industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop your technical, writing, and presentation skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;When you apply to our internship program, you will be considered for a variety of teams based on your interests and experience and our business needs.&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;What&#39;s Required&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Currently pursuing a bachelor&#39;s degree&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in the asset management industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to manage multiple tasks and deadlines in a fast-paced environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical, writing, verbal communication, and technical skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to work cooperatively with all levels of the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate professionalism and integrity in all interactions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitment to the highest ethical standards&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Team Overviews&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Corporate Communications team manages the global reputation of Point72 and all related entities. The team is responsible for all aspects of corporate communications, including media relations, external and internal communications, digital content and distribution, and brand management. This team works closely with Point72 senior management, functional leaders, and all departments firmwide.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Compliance department is an industry-leading team of compliance professionals who support global investment and trading activities by establishing and enforcing the firm&#39;s compliance policies, providing real-time advice, and conducting pre- and post-trade surveillance.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Facilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;MuiPaper-root MuiPaper-elevation MuiPaper-rounded MuiPaper-elevation0 MuiAccordion-root MuiAccordion-rounded Mui-expanded MuiAccordion-gutters css-ydipq2&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;MuiCollapse-root MuiCollapse-vertical MuiCollapse-entered css-1cbf1l2&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;MuiCollapse-wrapper MuiCollapse-vertical css-15830to&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;MuiCollapse-wrapperInner MuiCollapse-vertical css-9vd5ud&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;MuiAccordion-region css-1xdhyk6&quot;&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;MuiAccordionDetails-root css-l9xe8y&quot;&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;MuiTypography-root MuiTypography-body2 css-yhcg9n&quot;&gt;The Facilities team delivers a high level of corporate services to our offices around the globe, including real estate, property management, construction project management, day-to-day operations, maintenance, and security.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;MuiFormControl-root MuiFormControl-fullWidth css-17qa0m8&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Finance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Finance team provides a broad range of timely, accurate, relevant, and objective financial information, advice, and services to its business partners across Corporate Accounting, Global Payments, Procurement, FP&amp;amp;A, and Financial Reporting, with commitment to the highest professional and ethical standards.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Human Capital&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As an HR Team, our mission is to be trusted business partners and advisors within the Point72 community, committed to driving a distinctive culture that values collaboration, innovation, and adaptive performance. We are a group of professionals who prioritize business context while listening to all sides, across teams and levels, with empathy. We strive to be commercial and innovative, focused on deeply understand the nuances of global and business unit dynamics and seeking unconventional ways of approaching our relationships with our people.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Legal&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Legal team&#39;s mission is to deliver exceptional legal services in a manner that promotes the firm&#39;s performance with the utmost integrity. Our Legal department supports all Point72 groups globally with practical advice on a variety of complex legal and regulatory matters in an ever-changing, dynamic environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational Risk&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Operational Risk group is responsible for identification, monitoring, and reporting of operational risk across the firm. We also manage business continuity, third-party risks, and commercial lines of insurance (excluding employee benefits).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Operations team supports all operational aspects of trade processing, reconciliation, financing, and reporting firmwide for all products, including equities, derivatives, bonds, foreign exchange and futures, and digital assets across global markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regulatory Reporting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Regulatory Reporting team provides governance across all regulatory filings and related obligations globally. The team is responsible for report preparation, generating and coordinating responses for large cross-departmental filings, oversight of technology supporting regulatory filings, identification and implementation automation opportunities, and administering data standards. Regulators include but are not limited to the Securities and Exchange Commission (SEC), Commodity Futures Trading Commission (CFTC), National Futures Association (NFA), Monetary Authority of Singapore (MAS), Financial Conduct Authority (FCA), Securities and Futures Commission (SFC), and Kanto Finance Bureau (KFB).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategic Implementation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Strategic Implementation team drives the end-to-end delivery of large-scale, cross-functional initiatives that enable business growth and effective change management in alignment with the firm&#39;s long-term vision. Partnering with leaders across the firm, the team ensures alignment, operational readiness, and thoughtful risk management for new business activities and enterprise programs at every stage. The team plays a critical role in delivering the programs that fuel growth, innovation, and operational excellence firmwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Strategy team is a multidisciplinary group that partners directly with the firm&#39;s businesses to identify, design, and lead value-creating strategic business initiatives. We enable the development of new businesses, engage in special projects, and support the firm&#39;s strategic planning process. We also source, negotiate, and manage the firm&#39;s data assets, building a unified foundation that supports our investment professionals and the firm&#39;s growing data and AI ambitions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Treasury&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Treasury team supports the firm&#39;s credit and treasury functions across Central Funding, Securities Lending, and Broker Relations—verifying and disputing margin calls, reporting on counterparty exposure, investing excess cash, and negotiating margin terms with prime brokers and derivative counterparts. This work spans a range of asset classes, including equities, derivatives, bonds, foreign exchange, and futures, across global markets.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;About Point72&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Point72 is a leading global alternative investment firm led by Steven A. Cohen. Building on more than 30 years of investing experience, Point72 seeks to deliver superior returns for its investors through fundamental and systematic investing strategies across asset classes and geographies. We aim to attract and retain the industry&#39;s brightest talent by cultivating an investor-led culture and committing to our people&#39;s long-term growth. For more information, visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://point72.com/&quot;&gt;https://point72.com/&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The annual base salary is $75,000 (USD) which will be prorated based on internship start and end date. Actual compensation offered to the successful candidate may vary from posted hiring based upon geographic location, work experience, education, and/or skill level, among other things.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Payroll Specialist, United States Payroll&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A Career with Point72’s Finance Team &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Finance team provides a broad range of timely, accurate, relevant, and objective financial information, advice, and services to its business partners, with commitment to the highest professional and ethical standards. Our team offers a dynamic and collaborative environment where our colleagues can learn at a fast pace and are rewarded with advanced opportunities both within Finance and across the firm.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Payroll Specialist for the U.S. Payroll who will have direct ownership of hands-on payroll processing in addition to providing subject matter expertise and oversight. Specifically, you will:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end U.S. payroll processing with minimal supervision, including data gathering, validation, review, and final sign-off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead complex payroll activities such as multi-state tax calculations, W-2 testing and reconciliation, 401(k) processing, salary variance analysis, and retroactive adjustments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the U.S. payroll subject matter expert, providing guidance on federal, state, and local tax matters and ensuring compliance and accuracy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Independently prepare, review, and post payroll journal entries, including accruals, reversals, and adjustments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the primary point of contact for payroll escalations, employee inquiries, client questions, and external vendor coordination&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Human Resources (HR), Finance, Tax, and Benefits teams to resolve payroll issues, support audits, and manage cross-functional dependencies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review payroll outputs for quality and compliance, proactively identifying, investigating, and remediating discrepancies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive payroll process improvements, automation, system enhancements, and transitions using tools such as Excel, Workday, and other reporting/automation solutions, while mentoring junior team members as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What’s required? &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree or equivalent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;4+ years of finance, accounting, and/or U.S. payroll experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong hands-on expertise in state and local tax calculations and compliance, W-2 testing, year-end reconciliation, and corrections, 401(k) and benefits-related payroll processing, and salary variance analysis, reconciliations, and exception handling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced MS Excel proficiency, including VLOOKUP and XLOOKUP, COUNTIFS and SUMIFS, and nested IFs and complex reconciliation logic&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of US federal, state, and other jurisdictional payroll taxes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced experience with payroll-related journal entries, accruals, and financial reconciliations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to independently collect, validate, and review payroll data&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing payroll for foreign or global clients or working within a global service delivery model&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent attention to detail with a process-oriented approach to payroll compensation for some of the top leading professionals in the industry&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to efficiently analyze sizeable amounts of data and work with the Technology team to identify opportunities where improvement is essential&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to excel in a dynamic, fast paced environment and work effectively under pressure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A willingness to manage change and build working relationships with our clients within Finance and throughout the firm&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong verbal and written communication skills (English language verbal and writing skills)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent organizational skills to meet deadlines and manage multiple priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitment to the highest ethical standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT POINT72 &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Point72 is a leading global alternative investment firm led by Steven A. Cohen. Building on more than 30 years of investing experience, Point72 seeks to deliver superior returns for its investors through fundamental and systematic investing strategies across asset classes and geographies. We aim to attract and retain the industry’s brightest talent by cultivating an investor-led culture and committing to our people’s long-term growth. For more information, visit https://point72.com/&lt;/p&gt;

Stripe::gh_stripe_8128011.description:
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Stripe&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Stripe is a financial infrastructure platform for businesses. Millions of companies—from the world’s largest enterprises to the most ambitious startups—use Stripe to accept payments, grow their revenue, and accelerate new business opportunities. Our mission is to increase the GDP of the internet, and we have a staggering amount of work ahead. That means you have an unprecedented opportunity to put the global economy within everyone’s reach while doing the most important work of your career.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To further this important mission, we are building the foundation for a long-term talent bench at Stripe. We believe every campus hire can build products with meaningful impact at Stripe, and provide a far-reaching impact for anyone trying to grow their business online. We are looking for a University Recruiter to join our team to attract and hire the very best junior talent, while providing each candidate with an exceptional experience. This is a 11 month fixed term contract.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re a small but mighty team, and are committed to big results. You will help shape the future of our early-stage programs and be responsible for all parts of the campus recruiting life cycle, including, but not limited to, organizing and leading on campus events, driving a strong and diverse candidate pipeline, branding, building relationships with internal stakeholders, and managing our global internship program. You must be a builder who thrives in a learning environment - unafraid to try new things, embrace new ideas, and welcome suggestions for how we can iterate on our processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Partner closely with Stripe’s engineering organization to build the foundation of our early-stage university program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Manage the full-cycle recruiting process for new graduate and intern candidates across multiple roles and offices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Develop deep relationships with university groups, including faculty and student organizations, to design school-specific strategies that enhance our value proposition and brand on campus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Plan and execute on campus events with a focus on early engagement, education, and strategic branding&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Screen candidates and ensure that our hiring process is consistent and inclusive&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Drive a positive candidate experience for every new graduate and intern candidate considering a career at Stripe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Build and iterate on our year-round internship program alongside teammates and cross-functional stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Act as a resource to interns from hire to full-time conversion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Proactively share data-centric updates with internal stakeholders to maintain aligned decision making and build trusted partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for someone who meets the minimum requirements to be considered for the role. If you meet these requirements, you are encouraged to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A minimum of 5+ years full-cycle university recruiting experience in a fast-paced, high-growth environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A passion for building teams and delivering exceptional candidate experienceExcellent verbal and written communication skills, with an appropriate blend of professionalism and friendliness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Proven abilities to create a strategic campus strategy and build a diverse pipeline&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;An active and data-driven approach to problem solving; you may enjoy making sense of the trends and using the insights to better your process to make it more efficient&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A growth mindset and truly flexible. You can shift tasks and priorities with circumstances change (At a fast-growing startup, they often do)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;An interest in working in a cross-functional and fluid environment, the ability to learn quickly, and no desire to take yourself too seriously (a wry sense of humor is always appreciated!)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Ability and willingness to travel up to 30% during peak recruiting cycles and work flexible hours as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;You should include these in your application:&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A description of your relevant background and interests&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Your resume&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

