Engineers Gate::gh_engineersgate_8233715.description:
&lt;p&gt;Engineers Gate is a leading quantitative investment firm focused on systematic trading in global financial&amp;nbsp;markets. Our team of researchers, developers, and financial industry professionals apply sophisticated&amp;nbsp;statistical and machine learning models to uncover predictive signals in data and turn them into superior&amp;nbsp;investment returns. We believe that career fulfilment and enterprise success converge when smart, hard-working, and intellectually curious people come together in pursuit of innovation and excellence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Quantitative Developer will join our London Portfolio Management group and play a key role in building and scaling its central infrastructure. The work spans greenfield projects as well as enhancing and refactoring existing systems, offering immediate group-wide impact and exposure to every area of the trading system and research platform. We place a high value on continuous learning, and this role is a rare opportunity to work alongside and learn from highly experienced quantitative developers and researchers in a collaborative and innovative group. A successful candidate will combine strong numerical and engineering skills with a genuine appetite for learning new technologies. They will be comfortable working independently from high-level guidance. If you thrive in a collaborative environment, follow best practice across the full software development life cycle, and want to make a meaningful impact, we encourage you to apply.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build, maintain, and monitor the existing live trading infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and enhance the research platform and analytics tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with researchers to bring new trading strategies into production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills, Qualifications and Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Undergraduate degree in Computer Science or a related STEM discipline.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Production-level software engineering experience in a high-quality, technology-driven environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid understanding of algorithms, software architecture, design patterns, and software engineering best practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in at least one modern programming language (e.g. Python, C++, Java).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong numerical reasoning and problem-solving skills, with the ability to work comfortably with quantitative and scientific problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desirable Skills and Experience (beneficial but not required)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Python and/or MATLAB for numerical and scientific computing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AI-assisted development tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with machine learning and quantitative research workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to cloud platforms, especially AWS&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

