Hudson River Trading (HRT)::gh_wehrtyou_.description:
&lt;p&gt;Hudson River Trading (HRT) is seeking exceptional full-time PhD students to join our Algorithm Development teams in New York, London, and Singapore. Algorithm Developers at HRT are responsible for building and maintaining the models that drive our trading. A typical day involves applying rigorous statistical analysis to vast quantities of market and financial data to produce predictive trading models.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will work alongside fellow Algorithm Developers and Software Engineers to research, develop, and test novel order execution and model training methods to increase trading efficiency. This will involve running models live on our high-performance trading infrastructure and analyzing daily performance to maintain ongoing profitability. You can expect to apply your advanced academic research experience and expertise to impactful real world problems in trading across time horizons and machine learning strategies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ideal candidates are excited to apply their research expertise to identify new opportunities in worldwide markets, enjoy both self-guided research and collaborating with others to analyze and fix problems efficiently, and are critical thinkers who can learn and implement new skills in a fast-changing environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You are a full-time PhD student in a quantitative discipline (math, physics, computer science, statistics, or a related program) who is eligible for full-time roles in 2027&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in Python&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with statistical analysis, numerical programming, or machine learning in Python,&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pandas/Numpy, R, and/or MATLAB&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Brilliant analytical and problem-solving skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work creatively and independently on long-term technical problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Base salary for US is $300,000. Other locations have similarly locally competitive base salaries. A sign-on and discretionary performance bonus will be provided as part of the total compensation package, in addition to company-paid medical and/or other benefits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We do not allow multiple applications. Please apply to the ONE role you are most interested in and we will consider you for all open positions when reviewing your application.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Culture&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-value=&quot;{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:2,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;Hudson River Trading (HRT) brings a scientific approach to trading financial products. We have built one of the world&#39;s most sophisticated computing environments for research and development. Our researchers are at the forefront of innovation in the world of algorithmic trading. \n\nAt HRT we come from a variety of disciplines: mathematics and computer science, physics, and engineering, media and tech. We’re a community of self-starters who are motivated by the excitement of being at the cutting edge of automation in every part of our organization - from trading, to business operations, to recruiting and beyond.  Our culture celebrates great ideas whether they come from HRT veterans or new hires.  At HRT we’re friends and colleagues – whether we are sharing a meal, playing the latest board game, or writing elegant code. We embrace a culture of togetherness that extends far beyond the walls of our office.\n\nFeel like you belong at HRT? Our goal is to find the best people and bring them together to do great work in a place where everyone is valued. HRT is proud of our diverse staff; we have offices all over the globe and benefit from our varied and unique perspectives. HRT is an equal opportunity employer; so whoever you are we’d love to get to know you.&amp;quot;}&quot; data-sheets-userformat=&quot;{&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:13185,&amp;quot;3&amp;quot;:{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:0},&amp;quot;10&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;11&amp;quot;:4,&amp;quot;12&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;15&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;IBM Plex Sans&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;16&amp;quot;:11}&quot; data-sheets-textstyleruns=&quot;{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:0}{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:328,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:{&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:2,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:16711935}}}{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:402}{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:917,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:{&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:2,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:16711935}}}{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:945}&quot;&gt;Hudson River Trading (HRT) brings a scientific approach to trading financial products. We have built one of the world&#39;s most sophisticated computing environments for research and development. Our researchers are at the forefront of innovation in the world of algorithmic trading. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;At HRT we welcome a variety of expertise: mathematics and computer science, physics and engineering, media and tech. We’re a community of self-starters who are motivated by the excitement of being at the cutting edge of automation in every part of our organization—from trading, to business operations, to recruiting and beyond. We value openness and transparency, and celebrate great ideas from HRT veterans and new hires alike. At HRT we’re friends and colleagues – whether we are sharing a meal, playing the latest board game, or writing elegant code. We embrace a culture of togetherness that extends far beyond the walls of our office.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Feel like you belong at HRT? Our goal is to find the best people and bring them together to do great work in a place where everyone is valued. HRT is proud of our diverse staff; we have offices all over the globe and benefit from our varied and unique perspectives. HRT is an equal opportunity employer; so whoever you are we’d love to get to know you.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Please be advised: Use of AI tools by an applicant during interviews or assessments is strictly prohibited, unless otherwise instructed or agreed upon. We employ various methods to evaluate the authenticity of candidate responses. If we determine that AI assistance was used by an applicant during an interview or an assessment, we reserve the right to immediately end the interview or assessment, disqualify the applicant’s candidacy and/or rescind any job offers extended.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-value=&quot;{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:2,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;Hudson River Trading (HRT) brings a scientific approach to trading financial products. We have built one of the world&#39;s most sophisticated computing environments for research and development. Our researchers are at the forefront of innovation in the world of algorithmic trading. \n\nAt HRT we come from a variety of disciplines: mathematics and computer science, physics, and engineering, media and tech. We’re a community of self-starters who are motivated by the excitement of being at the cutting edge of automation in every part of our organization - from trading, to business operations, to recruiting and beyond.  Our culture celebrates great ideas whether they come from HRT veterans or new hires.  At HRT we’re friends and colleagues – whether we are sharing a meal, playing the latest board game, or writing elegant code. We embrace a culture of togetherness that extends far beyond the walls of our office.\n\nFeel like you belong at HRT? Our goal is to find the best people and bring them together to do great work in a place where everyone is valued. HRT is proud of our diverse staff; we have offices all over the globe and benefit from our varied and unique perspectives. HRT is an equal opportunity employer; so whoever you are we’d love to get to know you.&amp;quot;}&quot; data-sheets-userformat=&quot;{&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:13185,&amp;quot;3&amp;quot;:{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:0},&amp;quot;10&amp;quot;:1,&amp;quot;11&amp;quot;:4,&amp;quot;12&amp;quot;:0,&amp;quot;15&amp;quot;:&amp;quot;IBM Plex Sans&amp;quot;,&amp;quot;16&amp;quot;:11}&quot; data-sheets-textstyleruns=&quot;{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:0}{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:328,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:{&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:2,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:16711935}}}{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:402}{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:917,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:{&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:2,&amp;quot;2&amp;quot;:16711935}}}{&amp;quot;1&amp;quot;:945}&quot;&gt;You can review our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.hudsonrivertrading.com/global-applicant-privacy-notice/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Global Applicant Privacy Notice&lt;/a&gt;, which explains how we process applicant information.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

Maven Securities::gh_mavensecuritieshold.description:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Graduate Quant Researcher Program Chicago 2027&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Maven Securities is a leading proprietary trading firm that leverages sophisticated technology and quantitative analysis to trade in global financial markets. We specialize in options and derivatives market making, where your skills can be directly applied to have a real impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Maven, we believe exceptional careers are built deliberately. Our graduate program is designed for a small number of high-potential individuals each year, combining comprehensive training, real responsibility, and long-term development. We don’t hire large classes with the expectation that only a few will succeed, we invest in every individual who joins the team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Program details:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Chicago (based in London for training period)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Program start date:&lt;/strong&gt; September 6th, 2027&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Application deadline:&lt;/strong&gt; Rolling basis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Base salary: $150,000-175,000 dependent on education and experience&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll begin with a structured 7-week training program in London, designed to prepare you for a career in quantitative research. This initial phase focuses on building the technical foundations and professional skills needed for the role, as well as forming crucial working relationships with your UK counterparts - both on the Graduate Program and more senior stakeholders.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Following training, you’ll return to Chicago and roll onto two project rotations, where you’ll continue to learn through hands-on experience. Maven offers a few days of leave to support this transition, as well as travel, accommodation and relocation support.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will be doing:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, evaluate and continuously improve our automated trading algorithms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build quantitative pricing models, for example American Option Pricing and Volatility Modeling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Research and analyze trading data to find and test trading opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How and what you will learn:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Progress through a structured onboarding program with clear learning milestones&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build your foundation through theory and exercise-led training, led by Maven’s Head of Technology Training &amp;amp; Graduates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn about financial markets, our platforms and specific quant research field for OMM, apply your academic research abilities and learn how to perform research on real-world data of varied volume and sampling frequency across a variety of domains&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We will teach you how to use and master Maven’s in-house tools and systems. Maven utilizes the latest technology in order to meet and exceed our demanding business challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attend regular check-ins with the Quant Researcher and Emerging Talent teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key criteria:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A Bachelor’s, Master’s or PhD student in applied mathematics, statistics, engineering or physics&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant programming experience in at least one language (Python, C++, C#)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactive interest in improving existing trading strategies and identifying new opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Motivated for quantitative research, financial services and trading, with knowledge of financial markets&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A willingness to adopt and utilise emerging AI technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re looking for someone who is:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An entrepreneurial thinker&lt;/strong&gt; with the ability to generate ideas, take initiative and drive innovation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A critical problem solver and decision maker&lt;/strong&gt; who can analyze situations, think clearly and make effective decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An agile learner&lt;/strong&gt; who is able to quickly acquire knowledge, take on feedback, adapt and apply insights across different contexts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Able to synthesize information&lt;/strong&gt;, resolve conflicting inputs, see the bigger picture, and translate complex information into actionable recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaborative and influential&lt;/strong&gt;, able to build trust, work effectively with others and positively impact the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Results-focused and accountable&lt;/strong&gt;, taking ownership and delivering outcomes reliably&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Maven?:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dedicated In-House Trainers: &lt;/strong&gt;Gain the tools to succeed in a rapidly evolving market, where AI is integral to our strategy and daily operations. Our tailored curriculums are led by in-house experts and cover both technical and professional skills, as well as guidance on how to adopt AI best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accelerate Your Career: &lt;/strong&gt;Every permanent colleague receives a dedicated learning and development budget, full access to our online learning platform, and frequent training sessions led by our Maven experts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Proven Pathways: &lt;/strong&gt;Benefit from our structured pipeline programs that set you up for long-term success. Around a quarter of Maven’s workforce joined through an Emerging Talent Program, with many staying from Spring Week through the Graduate Program and beyond&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Supported to Succeed: &lt;/strong&gt;We are committed to fostering an inclusive workplace where everyone can perform at your best. We offer recruitment support where needed, and employee resource groups that help build community across the firm&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Grow with Guidance: &lt;/strong&gt;Enjoy regular feedback, structured review points, and informal off-desk chats. Everyone in our Emerging Talent Programs is also paired with a Maven buddy for practical advice and day-to-day support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Make a Real Impact, Fast: &lt;/strong&gt;From the start of the projects, you’ll be embedded in the team and learn directly from other Quant Researchers. After this, you’ll transition onto a permanent position within the team, where you’ll continue building upon the skills taught in the program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Please note:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We accept one application per candidate, per recruitment cycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Visa sponsorship is available for selected roles, please see our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.mavensecurities.com/emerging-talent/&quot;&gt;FAQ page&lt;/a&gt; for details&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Maven is an equal opportunity employer. We encourage applications from candidates of all backgrounds, and do not discriminate on the basis of race, religion, color, national origin, sex, gender, gender expression, sexual orientation, age, marital status, veteran status, disability status, or any other basis protected by applicable law.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits at Maven&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a graduate joining Maven, you’ll be eligible for a range of benefits, including:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;25 days of PTO plus US national holidays, which we expect you to take&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Private medical and dental cover, eye care support, life assurance, 401k or Roth retirement plans, and an Employee Assistance Program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consideration for a discretionary annual bonus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An annual learning and development budget, alongside wider training and development opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wellness benefits, including free use of the building gym and access to ClassPass&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Frequent social events, from welcome dinners and summer parties to company sports leagues and boat tours!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Daily breakfast in the office and a lunch allowance, plus snacks and drinks throughout the day&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced family-friendly policies, including maternity, paternity, adoption, fertility and partner’s leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work in a forward-thinking environment where AI is integral to our strategy and daily operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;

Verition Fund Management::gh_veritiongro.description:
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Firm Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Verition Fund Management LLC (“Verition”) is a multi-strategy, multi-manager hedge fund founded in 2008. Verition focuses on global investment strategies including Credit, Fixed Income &amp;amp; Macro, Convertible &amp;amp; Volatility Arbitrage, Event-Driven, Equity Long/Short &amp;amp; Capital Markets, and Quantitative Strategies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a quant developer of one of our world class quant trading teams, you’ll have the opportunity to get exposed to all aspects of the business; data ingestion, high-performance processing, features and modelling, portfolio and risk management, live execution and post-trade analysis.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and develop various tools in Python that will be crucial for analysis, research, trading, and risk management purposes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure integrity of data management pipeline and the underlying data itself, and actively identify, diagnose, and remedy data issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide ongoing maintenance, support, and enhancements for existing systems and platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate regularly with team managers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally with internal tech and data teams, researchers, traders, and outside vendors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commitment to safeguarding team information and adhering to business sensitivity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay abreast of market trends and academic research to continually adapt and refine trading strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement machine learning and other advanced techniques to enhance predictive accuracy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At least 1-3 years experience in Python programming, ideally including libraries relevant to data analysis and machine learning&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong background in data structures, algorithms, and object-oriented programming&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ideally a degree in Computer Science or some other STEM program&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with AWS or other cloud technology is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional analytical abilities and a strong problem-solving mindset&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication skills to effectively collaborate with traders and other team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of additional OOP languages like C++ or Java is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with machine learning and AI applications in trading is also a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High level of intellectual curiosity, strong work ethic, and a keen attention to detail.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work effectively in a team-oriented, fast-paced, and dynamic environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$100,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$200,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

